course: dictionary
lesson: 12799
title: The word electronically
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Electronically is an adverb. It tells you how something is done. It means by using electronic devices, such as computers, phones or the internet, or by using electricity and electronic parts instead of doing it by hand. «The homework was sent electronically to my teacher.» Here, the homework went through a computer or phone, not on paper.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Mum paid the bill electronically, on her phone.» The words on her phone tell you what electronically means: she used a device and did not pay with cash. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Electronically can also describe machines. «The garage door is electronically controlled, so a button opens it.» No one pushes or lifts the door by hand. Electricity and electronic parts do the work. Use the same clue-hunting every time you meet a new word.
fact: Electronically means by using electronic devices, or by using electricity and electronic parts.
fact: «Electronically» tells you how something is done, so it is an adverb.
fact: «The photos were shared electronically.» This means they were sent by phone, computer or the internet.
fact: «The lights were electronically controlled.» This means electronic parts switched them on and off, not hands or moving parts.
fact: When money is paid or sent electronically, keep your passwords private to keep it safe.
exercise: «The homework was sent electronically to my teacher.» What does electronically mean here? | * By using a computer, phone or the internet | By walking to school | Very slowly | By hand, with pen and paper
exercise: «The garage door is electronically controlled, so a button opens it.» What does electronically suggest? | Made of wood | * Using electricity and electronic parts, not moved by hand | Opened by a strong wind | Painted in bright colours
exercise: Ella asks, «Why should I take care when I pay electronically?» What is the best answer? | Because paying is always free | Because the bank is always closed | * Because your passwords keep your money safe | Because money cannot be sent
test: «Grandma sent her birthday card electronically this year.» What does electronically mean? | * By using a phone or computer | By painting it by hand | By posting it in a red box | With a big bow on it
test: «The fountain is electronically controlled and turns on at noon.» Which clue helps most? | Turns is a verb | * Controlled, so electronic parts switch it on | Noon is a time of day | The fountain is old
exam: «The school letters are now sent electronically, not on paper.» Which words show that electronically means by using a device? | The letters are now sent | School letters | * Sent electronically, not on paper | Now
